{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  Snippet: Global compare float (floating "Compare (3)" button)
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A tab fixed to the side of the screen, at the vertical middle:

                                              ┌────┐
                                              │ ⇄  │
                                              │ (3)│  ← number of products in compare
                                              │ C  │
                                              │ o  │  ← "Compare", written vertically
                                              │ m… │
                                              └────┘
  - Hidden until the shopper adds a product to compare; slides in then,
    "pops" when the number changes, slides out when compare is emptied.
  - Click → opens the compare page in a NEW TAB (target="_blank").
    Page: the page with the handle "compare" (/pages/compare).
  - 🗑 button under the tab: clears the whole compare list (no page change).
  - Not shown on the compare page itself.
  Phones: a smaller tab with the icon and number only.

  Settings: Theme settings > Product cards > "Floating compare button" (on/off)
            and "Floating compare button position" (right / left edge)

  Used in:  layout/theme.liquid
  CSS:      assets/global-product-card.css → "Floating compare button" (.compare-float*)
  JS:       assets/global-product-card.js → updateCompareFloat()
            (shows/hides it and sets the number from the saved compare list)
  Text:     locales → compare.float_text, compare.float_label,
            compare.float_clear, compare.float_cleared
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # The compare page: /pages/compare (or wherever the "compare" page lives)
  assign compare_url = pages.compare.url | default: '/pages/compare'
-%}

{%- if settings.compare_float_enable and settings.card_show_compare and template.suffix != 'compare' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Wrapper (fixed to the screen edge) holding two controls side by side in
    the tab — a link can't contain a button, so they are siblings:
    1. the link to the compare page (new tab)
    2. the 🗑 "Clear compare list" button (global-product-card.js empties
       the list, the tab slides out and a toast confirms)
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="compare-float compare-float--{{ settings.compare_float_position | default: 'right' }}"
    data-compare-float
    hidden
  >
    <a
      href="{{ compare_url }}"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
      class="compare-float__link"
      aria-label="{{ 'compare.float_label' | t: number: 0 }}"
      data-compare-float-link
      data-text-label="{{ 'compare.float_label' | t: number: '[number]' }}"
    >
      <span class="compare-float__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        {% render 'global-icon', name: 'compare', size: 20 %}
        <span class="compare-float__count" data-compare-total>0</span>
      </span>
      <span class="compare-float__text" aria-hidden="true">{{ 'compare.float_text' | t }}</span>
    </a>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="compare-float__clear"
      aria-label="{{ 'compare.float_clear' | t }}"
      title="{{ 'compare.float_clear' | t }}"
      data-compare-float-clear
      data-text-cleared="{{ 'compare.float_cleared' | t }}"
    >
      {% render 'global-icon', name: 'trash', size: 16 %}
    </button>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
